senses.gloss:
Rāṣṭra in the Rigveda^1 and later^2 denotes ‘kingdom’ or
‘royal territory.’
1) iv. 42, 1; vii. 34, 11; 84, 2;
x. 109, 3; 124, 4, etc.
2) Av. x. 3, 12; xii. 1, 8; xiii. 1, 35;
Vājasaneyi Saṃhitā, ix. 23; xx. 8;
Taittirīya Saṃhitā, i. 6, 10, 3; iii. 5,
7, 3; v. 7, 4, 4; Taittirīya Brāhmaṇa,
i. 2, 1, 13, etc.; Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā,
iii. 3, 7; 7, 4; 8, 6; iv. 6, 3.

Rāsabha in the Rigveda^1 and later^2 denotes an ‘ass.’
1) i. 34, 9; 116, 2; 162, 21; iii. 53, 5;
viii. 85, 7.
2) Taittirīya Brāhmaṇa, v. 1, 5, 7;
Kauṣītaki Brāhmaṇa, xviii. 1; Śata-
patha Brāhmaṇa, vi. 1, 1 11; 3, 1, 23;
2, 3; 4, 4, 3, etc.
Cf. Zimmer, Altindisches Leben, 233;
Geldner, Rigveda, Glossar, 149, who
suggests ‘mule’ as a possible sense in
Rv. iii. 53, 5.
